1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,105
Hello, and welcome to CyberGraph. Follow a security finding from its

2
00:00:05,105 --> 00:00:10,010
entry point to the code that matters. Inspect the graph, question its evidence,

3
00:00:10,069 --> 00:00:14,700
apply a repair, and recheck what remains. This demonstration uses

4
00:00:14,700 --> 00:00:19,582
public PyGoat training code, local analysis, and an interactive browser report.

5
00:00:20,283 --> 00:00:22,213
No language model is required.

6
00:00:24,020 --> 00:00:27,366
Start with Git and Python three point ten or newer.

7
00:00:28,065 --> 00:00:32,851
Clone CyberGraph, create and activate a virtual environment, then install the checkout

8
00:00:32,851 --> 00:00:37,422
using pip. In your IDE terminal, clone PyGoat and enter

9
00:00:37,422 --> 00:00:40,971
its folder. We pin the source for reproducibility.

10
00:00:41,672 --> 00:00:45,780
Run doctor to check setup. The dot means this repository.

11
00:00:46,482 --> 00:00:49,280
We never install or start the vulnerable application.

12
00:00:51,100 --> 00:00:56,160
Quickstart initializes configuration, builds the graph, analyzes risks, and writes a

13
00:00:56,170 --> 00:01:00,910
report. Python's abstract syntax tree identifies code structure;

14
00:01:00,980 --> 00:01:04,090
security rules and call resolution connect the entities.

15
00:01:04,790 --> 00:01:06,910
This run finds fourteen issues.

16
00:01:07,610 --> 00:01:09,800
Analyze records a history baseline.

17
00:01:10,500 --> 00:01:14,490
We then regenerate the visualization with source snippets and a larger node limit.

18
00:01:15,190 --> 00:01:16,620
No code is uploaded.

19
00:01:18,460 --> 00:01:23,850
Inside your repository, dot cybergraph contains the SQLite database and HTML report.

20
00:01:24,550 --> 00:01:27,580
Dot cybergraph dot TOML holds configuration.

21
00:01:28,280 --> 00:01:32,650
Quickstart also creates a GitHub Actions workflow: review it before committing.

22
00:01:33,350 --> 00:01:37,420
These export commands additionally create graph JSON and SARIF findings.

23
00:01:38,120 --> 00:01:40,480
Open report dot HTML in your browser;

24
00:01:40,540 --> 00:01:42,130
no web server is needed.

25
00:01:43,940 --> 00:01:49,510
The report uses HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and the bundled Cytoscape visualization

26
00:01:49,520 --> 00:01:52,690
library. A node represents a code entity;

27
00:01:52,760 --> 00:01:54,570
an edge represents a relationship.

28
00:01:55,270 --> 00:01:59,860
Blue marks entry points, green marks guards, and red marks sensitive sinks.

29
00:02:00,560 --> 00:02:02,740
Dashed regions group security layers.

30
00:02:03,440 --> 00:02:06,140
An amber trail highlights the selected attack path.

31
00:02:06,840 --> 00:02:12,680
Switch views for architecture, then use search, filters, and node selection to narrow your investigation.

32
00:02:14,500 --> 00:02:19,710
Select the SQL injection path: a Django route, its handler, and a raw database

33
00:02:19,730 --> 00:02:23,650
query. Click each node to inspect its role and connections.

34
00:02:24,350 --> 00:02:28,210
The path panel reports user-controlled input and no detected sanitizer.

35
00:02:28,910 --> 00:02:32,670
Its score prioritizes review, not exploitation probability.

36
00:02:33,370 --> 00:02:37,460
Reachability is evidence to investigate, not proof of a successful attack.

37
00:02:39,300 --> 00:02:44,250
Now inspect the source. The handler reads a name and password from the request.

38
00:02:44,950 --> 00:02:48,380
Line eight hundred and sixty-four concatenates them into SQL.

39
00:02:49,080 --> 00:02:52,670
Line eight hundred and seventy-eight sends the query to objects dot raw.

40
00:02:53,370 --> 00:02:57,540
An authentication check is present, but it does not prevent SQL injection.

41
00:02:58,240 --> 00:03:02,020
The file and line citations let a developer verify the finding directly.

42
00:03:03,820 --> 00:03:08,190
Back in the terminal, ask CyberGraph to trace this handler to its SQL sink.

43
00:03:08,890 --> 00:03:14,590
Explain returns a confidence level, the connected path, source citations, and repair guidance.

44
00:03:15,290 --> 00:03:18,650
This is local graph retrieval, not generated model reasoning.

45
00:03:19,350 --> 00:03:23,570
Inspect the cited evidence rather than treating an answer as a security guarantee.

46
00:03:25,420 --> 00:03:30,049
We also ran a small evidence ablation. Across nine seeded questions,

47
00:03:30,132 --> 00:03:34,715
two ordinary records contained both endpoint labels eight times; adding path records

48
00:03:34,715 --> 00:03:37,680
covered all nine and supplied connected citations.

49
00:03:38,382 --> 00:03:41,954
Ranking and limits were unchanged, but path records were longer.

50
00:03:42,656 --> 00:03:47,608
This measures evidence availability, not detection accuracy, model quality, or developer

51
00:03:47,608 --> 00:03:48,407
productivity.

52
00:03:50,220 --> 00:03:55,420
In our demonstration copy, replace concatenation with SQL placeholders and pass the values

53
00:03:55,430 --> 00:03:58,850
separately. Run analyze again, then history.

54
00:03:59,550 --> 00:04:04,770
The finding count falls from fourteen to thirteen: one finding fixed, no new findings.

55
00:04:05,470 --> 00:04:07,980
Finally, check the working-tree change.

56
00:04:08,680 --> 00:04:11,940
REVIEW flags remaining risks and configuration changes.

57
00:04:12,650 --> 00:04:16,460
A successful local repair does not make the entire application safe.

58
00:04:18,300 --> 00:04:22,976
Language models are optional. Anthropic, OpenAI, or Kimi

59
00:04:22,976 --> 00:04:26,108
can phrase the retrieved evidence and reference its citations.

60
00:04:26,810 --> 00:04:30,180
Enable a provider only when sharing that context is acceptable.

61
00:04:30,881 --> 00:04:33,632
Today's answers remain deterministic and offline.

62
00:04:34,333 --> 00:04:39,202
A model's explanation still needs verification; citation instructions do not guarantee

63
00:04:39,202 --> 00:04:44,668
accuracy. MCP and SARIF also support IDE and review integrations.

64
00:04:46,500 --> 00:04:51,200
Inspect, question, repair, and recheck. CyberGraph

65
00:04:51,200 --> 00:04:53,796
keeps evidence visible and the developer in control.

66
00:04:54,498 --> 00:04:55,653
Thank you for watching.
